id: pm-beads-lajb
title: Remove absolute host paths and non-public identities from the entire reachable Git history
description: "Read-only all-ref history inspection found 22 absolute-home-path patch lines across 11 reachable commits and six repository-relative PM/runtime files. Git author metadata also contains 106 commits across two non-noreply identities. This blocks merge and publication of new delivery work until a maintainer authorizes a coordinated history rewrite and all refs, PRs, tags, package artifacts, and consumers are revalidated."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[4]: history,privacy,publication-blocker,security
created_at: "2026-08-21T05:20:31.002Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-22T05:27:10.356Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-22T05:03:09.546Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-22T05:03:09.546Z"
claim_principal: ox-alpha
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: Obtain explicit maintainer authorization before destructive history rewriting; inventory every affected reachable ref and collaborator; create a recoverable backup; rewrite all affected path literals and disallowed identities consistently; force-update only the approved refs; invalidate or replace stale artifacts; rescan every reachable commit and blob with zero private path or disallowed identity findings; rerun package release and installed-artifact gates; re-review the exact rewritten head; document rollback and consumer re-clone instructions
risk: critical
confidence: high
reporter: codex
severity: critical
environment: pm-beads main d4f36b5; 190 reachable commits inspected across all local refs
repro_steps: Count git log --all patch lines matching absolute home paths; list affected repository-relative files without printing the private literals; classify git author emails as noreply or non-noreply without publishing the address values.
resolution: executed-history-rewrite
expected_result: "Public history and release artifacts contain no private host paths, personal identities, credentials, or private service data."
actual_result: Twenty-two absolute-home-path patch lines occur across eleven reachable commits and six PM/runtime files; 106 commits use two non-noreply author identities. Common secret-token patterns and sensitive filenames returned zero matches in the bounded scan.
component: public git history and release privacy
customer_impact: Merging or publishing from the current lineage could preserve private host context or personal identity indefinitely in public history and registry provenance.
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T05:03:09.107Z",ox-alpha,Executing maintainer-directed coordinated history rewrite per the pmc-t8tj precedent (pm-changelog PR #149).
close_reason: "Maintainer-directed coordinated history rewrite executed 2026-08-22 under Steve's standing release-privacy directive, replicating the pmc-t8tj precedent (pm-changelog PR #149). Disposable mirror /tmp/pmbeads-rewrite.git rewritten with git-filter-repo: email callback mapped both non-noreply identities to 1153461+unbraind@users.noreply.github.com across authors/committers/taggers; blob callback replaced the literal agent home path with $HOME in every blob. Pre-rewrite audit reproduced exactly: 22 host-path patch lines across 11 commits and 6 PM/runtime files, 106 commits on two non-noreply identities, zero credential-pattern matches. Post-rewrite verification: 0 host-path blobs across ALL objects (batch-all-objects scan), identity set noreply-only (unbraind, github-actions[bot], dependabot[bot]), ref-name inventory identical, HEAD tree byte-identical (ac2b86f). Force-push executed for all heads+tags via temporary admin protection lift, protection restored verbatim (test(22)/test(26) required, enforce_admins, conversation resolution). Fresh origin clone audit: all heads+tags clean, zero host-path objects, noreply-only identities. Residual risk documented: GitHub-managed refs/pull/* keep legacy objects fetchable by exact SHA until gc/support purge; normal clones never receive them."
body: ""
